::SPEECH_U05_L06_Quiz_Q01::
Question ID: SPEECH_U05_L06_Quiz_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.PRES.01
Question:
Digital presentation item 1: Which choice best supports coherent ideas in a speech presentation?
{
~A. Put the full speech paragraph on every slide#This choice does not fit the audience or purpose clearly enough. Check how word meaning or digital structure affects the listener.
~B. Use random images that do not support the point#This choice may sound related, but it does not fully support clear speech communication for the audience.
=C. Create slides with one clear focus connected to the central idea#Correct. This choice supports clear, audience-aware communication through precise word meaning or coherent digital presentation design.
~D. Add decoration that distracts from the message#This choice weakens the presentation because it ignores how the audience understands the message.
}
::SPEECH_U05_L06_Quiz_Q02::
Question ID: SPEECH_U05_L06_Quiz_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.SPK.01
Question:
Digital presentation item 2: Which choice best supports coherent ideas in a speech presentation?
{
=A. Use slide order that matches the speech organization#Correct. This choice supports clear, audience-aware communication through precise word meaning or coherent digital presentation design.
~B. Use random images that do not support the point#This choice may sound related, but it does not fully support clear speech communication for the audience.
~C. Arrange slides in an unrelated order#This choice reflects a misconception. Recheck tone, word meaning, slide organization, or presentation coherence.
~D. Add decoration that distracts from the message#This choice weakens the presentation because it ignores how the audience understands the message.
}
::SPEECH_U05_L06_Quiz_Q03::
Question ID: SPEECH_U05_L06_Quiz_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.PRES.02
